course: dictionary
lesson: 10767
title: Usually and how often
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Usually» means most of the time, but not every time. «I usually walk to school» tells you the walk happens on most days, so there may be a day when you go another way.
explain: Usually sits on a scale of how often things happen: always, usually, often, sometimes, rarely, never. Always means every time and never means not once. Usually is near the top, just below always.
explain: Context helps you here too. «The shop is usually open» tells you the shop is normally open, but it may close on a holiday. Ask yourself: is this every time, or most of the time? If it is most of the time, usually is the right word.
fact: «Usually» means in most cases, or as normally happens.
fact: «Usually» means most of the time, but not always.
fact: Frequency words show how often something happens: always, usually, often, sometimes, rarely, never.
fact: «Scary predictions online are usually nonsense meant to get attention.» Most of them are nonsense, but not all of them.
fact: «As usual» means the way it normally is, and «more than usual» means more than normal.
exercise: «I usually walk to school.» What does usually mean here? | Very quickly | *Most of the time | Only once | Never
exercise: «Coins thrown into a wishing fountain are usually collected for charity.» What does usually tell us? | No coin is ever collected | *Most coins are collected for charity, but not every one | Only one coin is collected | Every coin is collected, every time
exercise: Which word is closest to always, but not quite every time? | *usually | never | rarely | once
test: «The shop is usually open.» Does this mean the shop is open every single time? | It is open only on Sundays | Yes, every time without fail | *No, it is open most of the time | It is never open
test: «If you lose your place, staying calm and carrying on usually works.» What does usually suggest? | It works every time | *It works in most cases, but not always | It never works | It works only once
exam: Which word means in most cases, but not every time? | *usually | rarely | always | never
